shell:
    To compile the shell program, use the following commands:
    g++ -std=c++17 -pthread -o shell_program shell_program.cpp

    Run the compiled program with the following command:
    ./shell_program

    The shell supports wildcard character * in the mv and cp commands.
    The program measures the execution time for each command and displays it.

mv-threaded:

    This C++ program provides a file mover utility with multi-threading support. The program allows users to move files from a source directory to a destination directory, with the option to move multiple files concurrently.

    To compile the file mover program, use the following commands:
    g++ -std=c++17 -pthread -o file_mover file_mover.cpp

    Run the compiled program with the following command:    
    ./file_mover

    Supports moving files from a source directory to a destination directory.
    Multi-threaded operation for moving multiple files concurrently.
    Interactive mode (-i flag) for prompting before overwriting files in the destination.
    Measures the execution time for the file moving operation.


cp-threaded:

    This C++ program provides a file copying utility with multi-threading support. The program allows users to copy files and directories from a source location to a destination, with the option to copy multiple files concurrently.


    Supports copying files and directories from a source location to a destination.
    Multi-threaded operation for copying multiple files concurrently.
    Recursive copying (-r flag) for copying entire directories.
    Measures the execution time for the file copying operation.